Chromium 158.0.8127.36 spellcheck dictionary converter.

The .cc and .h files under chrome/ and third_party/ are copied from that
Chromium revision:

  chrome/tools/convert_dict/
  third_party/hunspell/google/

They write the .bdic files Helium's spellchecker downloads. stub/ supplies
the small parts of //base and MD5 that those files include, using system
ICU and libcrypto. hunspell_to_bdic.cc is the program the package runs.

dic_reader.cc no longer logs a missing .dic_delta. The myspell packages
do not ship one.

The bdic version suffix published by helium-services-refresh-dicts.sh has
to stay in step with GetVersionedFileName in

  components/spellcheck/common/spellcheck_common.cc

of the Chromium revision Helium is built from. Helium 0.22.3 uses
158.0.8127.36.

Rebuild the source archive after changing this directory:

  tar -C convert-dict -cf - . | zstd -T0 -19 -o helium-services-bdic.tar.zst
  abb store helium-services-bdic.tar.zst

The license for the Chromium files is LICENSE.bsd.
